  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Assistive Tech - Africa Mobility Pilot</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Access to Assistive Tech (AT) remains critically low across Africa. AT ventures face unique barriers that limit their growth: weak market data, low investor confidence, fragmented supply chains, high production costs, limited policy support and limited scale. Founders often bring strong technical skills but lack the networks, capital and business expertise needed for international expansion. This pilot responds directly to those challenges. It is designed to accelerate the internationalisation of AT ventures in Kenya, South Africa and Ghana while also building lasting connections within the three countries, drawing expertise from Asia and the UK.</narrative>
  </description>
